"new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKURAI, HISAO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KINPARA YOSHIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOYAMA MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUYAMA MIHO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKURAI HISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KINPARA, YOSHIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOYAMA, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUYAMA, MIHO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKURAI, HISAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A control device of an induction motor comprising a power inverter circuit (1), a current detector (3), a current component operation circuit (4) to operate first and second current components, a magnetic flux command operation circuit (5) to operate a magnetic flux command value that can set an amplitude ratio between the square of the first current component and the square of the second current component to a preset value, a voltage component command operation circuit (6) to operate a primary voltage component command value and a primary voltage command operation circuit (7), the current component operation circuit (4) operating the first current component in phase with the primary voltage component command value and the second current component shifted 90 DEG  in phase.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un dispositif de commande d'un moteur asynchrone, ce dispositif comprenant un onduleur (1), un détecteur (3) de courant, un circuit (4) de réalisation des composantes du courant servant à réaliser des première et seconde composantes de courant, un contrôleur (5) de flux magnétique servant à contrôler le flux magnétique pouvant établir un rapport d'amplitude entre les carrés des première et seconde composantes du courant, un contrôleur (6) de composante de tension servant à contrôler une composante de tension primaire, et un contrôleur (7) de tension primaire, le circuit (4) de réalisation des composantes du courant servant à réaliser la première composante du courant en phase avec la composante de tension primaire et la seconde composante du courant à décalage de phase de 90 DEG .</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>